{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>וְהִנֵּה קָמָה אֲלֻמָּתִי וְגַם נִצָּבָה.</b> This is a hint that first he would rule over them (מְשׁוֹל) and afterward reign as king (מְלוֹךְ), for there is no king without a multitude of people, and at present they were but few in number — over whom would he reign? But the expression מֶמְשָׁלָה, dominion, applies even over few people. Therefore he said 'וְהִנֵּה קָמָה אֲלֻמָּתִי' — a hint to the time of rising (קִימָה), when he would rise to rule, for the language of קִימָה speaks of the beginning of the matter, when a man rises up against his fellow to rule over him. 'וְגַם נִצָּבָה' is a hint to kingship, for then he would have a settled position (מַצָּב) and a populace (יִשּׁוּב), and to him alone would belong the kingship. And he spoke in the manner of 'not only this, but even that' (לֹא זוֹ אַף זוֹ), to say: not only dominion would I have, but even kingship would I have. But they reversed the matter and said 'הֲמָלֹךְ תִּמְלֹךְ עָלֵינוּ אִם מָשׁוֹל תִּמְשֹׁל בָּנוּ' (Genesis 37:8) — for not only kingship would you not have, but even ordinary dominion you would not have over us."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:12.800704998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}